{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostoncitywalks/items/26334/", "pk": 26334, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostoncitywalks/", "pk": 8278, "shortname": "bostoncitywalks", "name": "Boston City Walks", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "Downtown Freedom Trail Walk - History/Architecture", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 2, "unicode": "Downtown Freedom Trail Walk - History/Architecture", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": false, "sold_out_text": "", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-midnight", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 3.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_reached_hours": 0.0, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 1, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 2000, "description": "#Get to know and love Boston in just one morning!  \n\nCome explore the interesting streets, admire the architecture, and discover the history of downtown.  Hear stories that highlight Boston’s history and culture as we walk the Freedom Trail from Faneuil Hall to  Boston Common.  \n \nThis tour puts it all in context for you, from the time Boston was first settled to today’s quirky streets and mixed architecture!\n\n##Duration\n\n- 1.2 hours long\n\n\n##Tour Times\n\n- Daily at 10am\n\n\n##Highlights of this 70 minute guided tour include:\n\n-  The Old & New State House     \n-  Faneuil Hall           \n-  Boston Massacre Site \n-  Park Street Church                   \n-  King’s Chapel       \n-  Old South Meeting House\n-  Old Granary Cemetery             \n-  Old City Hall and First Schoolhouse Site\n-  The Old Corner Bookstore       \n-  Boston Common  \n-  The Irish Famine Memorial \n\n\n\n##Meeting Location\nThe NW corner of State & Congress Streets outside 28 State Street (The Citizens Bank Building)", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "**Important Notice:** Please arrive at least 10 minutes before your scheduled tour time, as tours depart right on time.\n\n**Meeting Location:** The tour will meet on the NW corner of State and Congress Streets, across from the Old State House outside 28 State Street. Your Boston CityWalks Tour Guide will have either a dark shirt or jacket with the \"Boston CityWalks\" name and a dark blue \"Boston CityWalks\" cap.\n\n**What to Wear**\n\nYou will be outside for much of the tour, so dress for the forecasted weather! We recommend layers, as the temperatures can become higher throughout the day. (It's easy to peel a layer off!)\nWear comfortable walking shoes.\nOn sunny days, we suggest you use sunscreen. Hats and sunglasses can also be helpful.\nIf the weather forecast calls for rain or showers, rain jackets, umbrellas and hats can help. On most tours, the guide will have emergency ponchos available in case of unexpected inclement weather.\n \n**What to Bring/What Not to Bring**\n\nWe suggest you bring a bottle of water with you. These can also be purchased at street vendors along the way. (If you intend to purchase water, be sure to bring some extra cash!)\nIf you have young children, it is highly recommended that you bring a folding carriage with you, as kids do get tired along the way.\nAnd of course, BRING YOUR CAMERA!!\n \n**Other Tips & Guidelines**\n\nPlease arrive at least 10 minutes before scheduled departure time.\nIf there are any particular types of things you would like to see or hear about, please get ready to let your guide know.\nIf you have any problems or questions prior to the tour, you can call our main number at 866-WE-WALKS. If you need to reach us close to tour time, call 508-904-2819.\nGratuities are not required, but certainly are welcome and appreciated!!\n\n-------------------------------\n\n#Other Activities We Recommend:\n[![Classic Harbor Line](https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/Sgos43OiTPmc7ezTYfyr)](https://fareharbor.com/boston-sailing/?asn=fareharbor&asn-ref=bostoncitywalks&ref=confirmationemail)\n[![Sail When and If](https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/BmuiEoSHq2U7N4rDtNyw)](https://fareharbor.com/sailwhenandif/?asn=fareharbor&asn-ref=bostoncitywalks&ref=confirmationemail)", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "1.2 Hours • Ages 5+ • Get to know and love Boston in just one morning!", "short_description": null, "image_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/6XYsQUfVThi67jOz8jci", "image_cdn_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/6XYsQUfVThi67jOz8jci", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostoncitywalks/items/26334/images/40409/", "pk": 40409, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/T69QG2ZnQKTkkdF0zbms", "image_cdn_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/T69QG2ZnQKTkkdF0zbms", "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostoncitywalks/"}, "item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostoncitywalks/items/26334/"}, "crop": {}, "cropped_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/T69QG2ZnQKTkkdF0zbms", "cropped_cdn_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/T69QG2ZnQKTkkdF0zbms", "is_low_resolution": true, "has_text_overlay": false, "has_logo_overlay": false}], "created_at": "2016-07-02T17:21:35+0000", "modified_at": "2025-08-05T19:29:31+0000", "is_gratuity_enabled": false, "is_sms_reminder_enabled": false, "receipt_footer": "", "is_scanning_enabled": false, "scanning_instructions": "", "external_url": "", "effect